I use autoquiver by default, and I think it's great.

however, it's a bit of a pain when my dagger wielding, dagger throwing
wizard decides to autoquiver a bunch of useless darts, even though he
has a stack of blessed +7 elven daggers in inventory.

I would suggest that the order of selection be changed a little.

First, the game must decide what type of available weapon to quiver.
Note that available means "not wielded":

-If the player is wielding a sling, bow, crossbow then rocks, arrows,
bolts be selected as appropriate. (It might do this already, I don't
know). Same for firearms in slashem, obviously.

-If the above doesn't apply, then the selection is made according to
the character's skill level: If I am expert in dagger but unskilled in
darts, then daggers please.

-If skill levels are equal, then whatever system is currently in use
should be applied.

Then the game might have to choose beteween multiple stacks of daggers/
bolts/ arrows/ whatever:

If bolts/ arrows/ darts/ rocks (which are all useless as hand-weapons),
then priority goes to the highest known non-cursed enchantment. If
enchantments are unknown or equal, then go by BUC status. If that is
also unknown or equal, then largest stack-size wins.

Daggers are a slightly different matter, since (if not already wielding
one) you may want to keep one back for melee. Therefore large stacks
should be given priority, but not if known to be cursed or
negatively-enchanted.
After that, decisions should be based on non-cursed status and
enchantment, in that order.

Just my 0.02 [insert local currency] worth.


